WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.040
Game of Thrones Season 8 Episode 2 is called
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.030
It’s the calm before the storm at Winterfell,
with characters celebrating life – before

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.900
the dead arrive.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.540
Jaime Lannister wants to help fight the white
walkers.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.230
But Daenerys and Sansa don’t trust him,
because he’s the brother of their enemy,

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.230
Cersei.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.669
Sansa’s mad because Jaime fought against
her family . And Daenerys is mad cause Jaime

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:29.369
killed her father , the Mad King, twenty years
ago.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:34.441
Jaime killed the king to save a city from
wildfire . But when Ned Stark found him at

00:00:34.441 --> 00:00:40.800
the Throne, he judged Jaime guilty , and ever
after, Jaime was hated as a Kingslayer, and

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.670
oathbreaker . And now, Jaime’s judged again,
by Ned Stark’s daughter, and the Mad King’s

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.790
daughter – his past is coming back to haunt
him.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.430
But this time, there’s someone who believes
in Jaime.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:58.950
Brienne says Jaime is an honourable man, that
he protected her, and kept his oaths.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:04.140
Brienne shows Jaime trust and respect like
no one ever has.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.569
So Jaime gets his sword back – Widow’s
Wail, one of the two Valyrian swords that

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:11.079
were melted down from Ned Stark’s old sword,
Ice.

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:14.369
The other sword, Oathkeeper, is used by Brienne.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:20.619
So in Jaime and Brienne, Ned’s sword is
symbolically reforged – his steel is protecting

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:26.600
House Stark once more – in the hand of the
man who he’d once judged guilty.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.549
Jaime reveals that Cersei lied – she’s
not gonna help the good guys, she’s just

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:35.609
wants to hold the Throne . Which means Tyrion
was wrong again – his whole plan of the

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:39.039
wight hunt and the peace summit was for Cersei’s
cooperation.

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:41.429
Turns out that was all for nothing.

00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:46.929
Tyrion has failed Daenerys over and over , so
she threatens to replace him as Hand . If

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:52.740
Tyrion can’t find purpose and self-worth
serving Daenerys, what will he do?

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.549
Jaime apologises to Bran, the boy he crippled
in Episode 1 . Bran didn’t tell anyone that

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:02.740
Jaime pushed him, cause if he did, the Starks
wouldn’t have let Jaime join them.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.920
Bran takes the philosophical view that if
Jaime hadn’t crippled him, Bran wouldn’t

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.580
have become the magic three-eyed raven, and
Jaime wouldn’t have become a heroic man.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.680
But Bran also makes an ominous comment that
there might not be an “afterwards” for

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.940
Jaime . You get the sense the Bran knows the
future – and he has had some visions of

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.640
the future before . But we don’t know the
full extent of his powers since he became

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.830
the raven.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.000
He says he can see “Everything that's ever
happened, to everyone” and “Everything

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.420
that's happening right now” – but the
visions are confused and fragmented . So in

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.030
practice, he’ll probably just know whatever’s
convenient to the plot at the time.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.810
Gendry works as a blacksmith, and Arya enjoys
the view – just like she did in Season 2.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:52.720
Gendry remembers Arya as this plucky young
girl, but Arya shows him she’s something

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.860
else now – closer to John Wick than Arry
the orphan boy . She talks about death , and

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.820
throws daggers, and Gendry’s impressed,
confused, and aroused.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:08.370
Later, Gendry brings the weapon Arya ordered
– a sort of staff, with dragonglass at both

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.370
ends.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:13.800
It’s like the weapon of Symeon Star-Eyes,
a legendary knight mentioned in the books.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.800
He had a double-ended staff , and he was blind
– just like Arya was blind.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.680
But there are also hints that Symeon was some
kind of white walker – he went to the Nightfort,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:30.290
and had “star sapphires” in his eyes , like
a walker’s eyes . In the last scene, Arya

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.430
asks Gendry how many wights he’s fought
. Now, she asks how many girls he’s had

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.780
sex with . Last scene was about death, this
scene’s about life.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.970
Arya doesn’t want to die a virgin – so
she and Gendry have sex.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.580
Arya has suffered so much death and darkness
– now she finally gets some love and light.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:54.510
But afterwards, Arya looks alone, while Podrick
sings of sorrow and pain.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:59.970
Arya had once asked Gendry to be her family
. But after everything she’s been through,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.310
Arya can’t reconnect.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:07.100
In the books, she says there’s a hole inside
her where her heart had been, that it will

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:12.910
“never feel any better” . A lot of people
were shocked to see Arya have sex, but no

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.949
one seemed to mind when she committed mass
murder – because our culture and morals

00:04:16.949 --> 00:04:19.200
are completely fucked.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.220
Jaime and Brienne make awkward small talk
about the left flank and the rise on the ground

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.180
until Brienne snaps, and basically asks what
is their relationship now?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.710
They used to hate each other, then they saved
each other, and now they’re starting to

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.280
love each other, and Brienne doesn’t know
how to handle that.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.889
Remember, when Brienne was young, some boys
pretended to like her.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:45.120
But it turned out to be a cruel joke – they
mocked her as “Brienne the Beauty”.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.419
So it makes sense that Brienne is suspicious
when a man shows her affection and respect

00:04:49.419 --> 00:04:55.130
– especially when Jaime was always so horrible
to her . So Jaime does something he’s never

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.250
done before.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:01.740
He humbly and sincerely submits himself to
Brienne, says he’s not a great fighter any

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:07.390
more, but he’d “be honored to serve”
her . Jaime rejects the pride and cruelty

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:13.020
that once defined him, and he honours the
woman who showed him how to be a better man.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.190
Also, we learn that Podrick is a badass now.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.260
Remember what a goober he was in Season 2?

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:22.790
This is the best character transformation
since Lancel Lannister.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:26.800
Jorah tells Daenerys that she should forgive
Tyrion’s mistakes.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.389
Jorah had wanted to be Daenerys’ Hand himself,
but he says that Tyrion is the right man for

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:32.630
the job.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.040
Jorah used to be jealous and controlling with
Daenerys.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:41.390
He undermined her other advisors, cause he
wanted her all to himself . Now, he’s grown

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:46.610
past that, and does whatever’s truly best
for Daenerys – he even accepts that Daenerys

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:53.270
loves Jon not him . Jorah’s become a better
man, his arc seems complete – which probably

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.020
means he’ll die next episode.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.889
Jorah also advises Dany to make peace with
Sansa.

00:05:59.889 --> 00:06:05.210
So Daenerys finds some common ground with
Sansa – they’re both powerful women with

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:11.330
“complicated” families . But Sansa is
suspicious that Dany is manipulating Jon – exploiting

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.870
his love for her political gain.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:19.010
Sansa knows that her brother Robb’s love
for Talisa led to his downfall . But Daenerys

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:22.570
argues that, if anything, Jon has manipulated
her.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:27.340
Daenerys came to Westeros to take the Iron
Throne, but Jon convinced her to come north

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:33.720
and fight walkers instead – Daenerys delayed
her life’s ambition partly out of love for

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:34.720
Jon.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.480
But Sansa asks what happens after the walkers
are defeated – cause Daenerys still wants

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:43.100
to rule Westeros, including the north.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:49.090
Sansa’s family fought and died to rule the
north themselves – Robb battled the Lannisters,

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.930
Sansa and Jon battled the Boltons, and Sansa
doesn’t want all that to be for nothing.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:58.500
She wants an independent north , and Daenerys
doesn’t want to give to her.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:03.870
She probably just should, though – she promised
the Greyjoys an independent Iron Islands , why

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.770
not an independent north?

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.320
This conflict feels kind of contrived.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.760
But the point is that Dany and Sansa understand
each other better now, but there’s still

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.060
tension.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.830
Theon Greyjoy arrives, and says he’ll fight
for the Starks . He wants to redeem himself

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.110
for betraying the Starks in Season 2.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:25.810
He and Sansa have an emotional hug.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:31.360
They survived Ramsay together – no one else
really understands what they went through.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:38.010
Sansa and Theon grew up like siblings at Winterfell,
and now they’re finally back home, together.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:39.660
Davos feeds the common folk.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:43.449
You’ve gotta feel sorry for these random
peasants who’ve been conscripted to fight

00:07:43.449 --> 00:07:45.250
in World War Z.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:49.370
Most of the real soldiers died in Robb’s
war, or the Battle of the Bastards.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:53.520
These hapless leftovers will be slaughtered
by the walkers.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.420
Gilly is also helping the commons.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:01.190
She started out so meek and afraid – now
she’s a confident and compassionate leader.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:05.720
She and Davos meet a girl called Teela, who’s
looks like Shireen – the girl who taught

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.060
Davos and Gilly how to read.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:12.300
Teela has a burn on her face, which looks
like Shireen’s greyscale – it’s also

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.570
a reminder that Shireen was burned.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:20.350
These are the sorts of people who will die
by the thousands when the walkers come – it’s

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:26.680
always the innocents who suffer most . Gilly
tells Teela to stay in the crypt during the

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.139
battle, because the crypt is safe.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:33.360
Five times this episode, we’re told that
the crypt is “safe” , which practically

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.270
guarantees that something awful will happen
there.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.710
The crypt is full of dead Starks, and the
white walkers can raise the dead, so maybe

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:45.980
recently dead Starks like Rickon will attack
– there are lots of hints in the books of

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:50.940
dead Starks rising . But most of the dead
in the crypt are very old, there wouldn’t

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.600
be bodies left.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:57.720
We have seen some spooky skeleton wights in
the past, but most of the dead Starks are

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:58.720
dust.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.040
So maybe there’s some other icy danger down
there.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:07.180
The books mention deeper, darker, ancient
levels to the crypt , which might hold some

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:11.460
terrible secret, like a captive Night’s
Queen or something.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:15.630
Or maybe there’s a secret entrance, so the
walkers could attack from within.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:19.690
Or maybe there’s protective magic and the
crypts really are safe.

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:24.170
Tormund Beric and Edd come to Winterfell,
and Jon gets a bear-hug from Tormund.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.910
They’ve had a crazy relationship.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:31.770
Jon once climbed the Wall with Tormund’s
wildings, then betrayed him, and fought against

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.750
him at the battle for Castle Black.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:38.640
Then, they fought together – at Hardhome,
Winterfell, and beyond the Wall.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.580
This wildling leader and Night’s Watchman
have become allies and friends.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:48.529
Tormund says the dead are coming, and everyone
one not at Winterfell is with them . The walkers

00:09:48.529 --> 00:09:53.480
have taken Last Hearth, and are almost at
Winterfell – so they could also have Karhold,

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:58.279
and the Dreadfort, and many little villages,
as well as all the wildling land.

00:09:58.279 --> 00:10:03.960
The army of the dead will be huge – and
Tormund says they’ll arrive tomorrow . So

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.330
Winterfell has new defences.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:10.750
The opening sequence shows trenches round
the castle, and the plan is to light them,

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:16.880
as a barrier of fire . Fire does stop wights
– the zombies – but it doesn’t stop

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:19.300
white walkers, the ice creatures.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:23.860
The walkers are vulnerable to dragonglass,
so there’s dragonglass on the walls, and

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:26.800
on caltrops, and there’s heaps of dragonglass
weapons.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.550
There’ve also got trebuchets, and traps.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:35.430
But the army of the dead is too big, the wights
don’t sleep or stop , and every human who’s

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.100
killed can be raised again as a wight.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.399
So everyone gets together and makes a plan.

00:10:41.399 --> 00:10:45.930
The walkers are led by the Night King, and
Jon hopes that if the Night King dies, all

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:50.700
the walkers and wights will die too . And
Bran says the Night King will come for him

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:56.110
. Bran was marked by the Night King in Season
6, it’s like a GPS tracker so he always

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.000
knows where Bran is.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.089
So they plan to use Bran as bait – putting
him in the godswood to lure the Night King.

00:11:03.089 --> 00:11:08.570
Theon and the ironborn will guard Bran , which
is cool cause there was foreshadowing in Season

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:13.630
1 that Theon would battle in the godswood
. This seems like the perfect setup for Theon

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.630
to heroically sacrifice himself.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:21.389
Jon says they’ll keep the dragons nearby,
to protect Bran and wait for the Night King

00:11:21.389 --> 00:11:27.180
– but they won’t use the dragons in the
field . Which seems really dumb.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:31.330
Dragons breathe fire – they’re not good
at protecting wheelchair-bound wizards in

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:36.089
flammable forests – they’re really good
at burning zombies.

00:11:36.089 --> 00:11:39.970
Surely the dragons are the only real hope
of stopping the dead – they shoulda flew

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.060
out and burned the dead before they even arrived.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:47.310
Maybe Dany and Jon are worried about the Night
King’s Olympic javelin skills.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:52.180
But that means relying on footsoldiers to
hold off an endless zombie horde long enough

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:56.420
to kill the Night King – assuming the Night
King even shows up.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:12:01.690
So like the wight hunt last season, this plan
is pretty ridiculous – it’s almost like

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:05.350
this is a TV show and it’s meant to be dramatic.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:10.040
The interesting bit is when Bran explains
the motivation of the white walkers.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:15.070
He says the Night King wants to “erase this
world” and bring “An endless night”.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:20.010
He specifically wants to kill Bran because
as the three-eyed raven, Bran is the world’s

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:25.080
memory – in the books, the magic of the
weirwoods stores the souls of the dead, and

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:31.680
remembers the history of the earth Sam says
that memory is what makes us human, and forgetting

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:37.710
is death . Thrones author George Martin is
a melancholy romantic . He’s been writing

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:43.730
for decades about ghosts and songs and lost
loves – all different echoes of the past.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.899
And that shines through in Game of Thrones.

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:51.360
The story is about vengeance and grief and
loyalty and guilt, all feelings that are rooted

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:54.410
in memories of loss and love.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:59.690
That's why the north remembers, why the Starks
treasure their crypts, why Ned Stark and Rhaegar

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:03.540
are still important characters even though
they’re long dead.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:08.190
Memory makes us human, so it makes sense that
the ultimate evil in this story is a metaphor

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.279
for forgetting our humanity.

00:13:10.279 --> 00:13:14.150
That said, it's all very fucken abstract.

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:17.180
Shouldn't the big bad guys have a more specific
motivation?

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:23.120
There are all these weird hints of baby sacrifice,
spooky spirals, ancient mystery.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:28.370
The books hint at ancient pacts, and secret
bloodlines, there’s Coldhands, and Joramun’s

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:33.190
Horn, the Five Forts, and Bloodstone Emperor
– surely that adds up to something more

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:35.100
than this metaphor.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:39.480
There may still be secrets to reveal about
the walkers – whether in this show, or the

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.550
prequel show, or in upcoming books.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.610
Tyrion speaks with Bran.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:50.100
It is crazy that Bran is apparently an omniscient
psychic know-it-all, yet no one asks him what

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.440
he knows, or what his powers are.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:58.040
Tyrion, at least, sees the value in knowledge,
so he asks to hear Bran’s story , but the

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.709
scene cuts before we hear anything.

00:14:00.709 --> 00:14:02.760
So what did Tyrion learn?

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:07.980
On the excellent Still Watching podcast, the
writer of this episode, Bryan Cogman, suggested

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:12.819
that Tyrion and Bran just talked about Bran’s
journey, nothing super important happened

00:14:12.819 --> 00:14:18.269
. But Tyrion does seem more optimistic about
the battle after speaking with Bran . Maybe

00:14:18.269 --> 00:14:22.280
Bran told him something that’ll help in
the fight.

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:25.850
Missandei says hi to some northern girls,
and they run off.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:30.120
She’s treated as an unwelcome foreigner
here, and Grey Worm says they should go somewhere

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.920
else after the war.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:37.450
Missandei wants to go back to Naath , her
homeland, where she lived before she was enslaved.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.700
The Naathi are called the Peaceful People
– they don’t eat meat, and don’t kill

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.750
people, even in self-defence.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:47.940
So they’re often attacked by slavers or
conquerors, but their enemies don’t last

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.940
long.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:54.060
Because Naath is full of butterflies that
carry a disease that kills outsiders.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:58.640
Of course that would mean they’d kill Grey
Worm, so maybe this is only true in the books.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:04.160
Point is, this is a touching moment of two
lovers dreaming of a happily ever after.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:09.440
So it’s the perfect setup for some heart-wrenching
tragedy next episode – maybe Grey Worm or

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.959
Missandei will die.

00:15:11.959 --> 00:15:15.220
Sam Edd and Jon talk on the walls of Winterfell.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:20.579
We finally see Jon’s direwolf Ghost – though
he’s still much smaller than in the books.

00:15:20.579 --> 00:15:27.000
The book-direwolves get huge , and have deep
symbolic and magic connections with each Stark.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.680
Jon Sam and Edd were in the Night’s Watch
together.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:34.660
Along with Grenn and Pyp and the rest, they
survived wildlings and wights and worse, but

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:39.971
now it’s just these three left . Sam and
Jon laugh at Edd for being a virgin, which

00:15:39.971 --> 00:15:41.490
is a bit rich.

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:46.450
The Night’s Watch oaths are understood to
mean having no sex – Jon and Sam broke that

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.450
rule.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:50.620
But the rules are out the window [like Bran]
now anyway, cause the Wall has fallen, and

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.720
the Night’s Watch all but dissolved.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:57.700
Still, Jon Sam and Edd keep the important
bits of their oath – they are the swords

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:02.820
in the darkness, the watchers on the walls,
the shield that guards the realms of men . The

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:07.980
Night’s Watch was founded thousand years
ago to defend the living from the dead.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:14.139
And tonight, everyone at Winterfell is Night’s
Watch . Tyrion and Jaime reflect on how far

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:15.139
they’ve come.

00:16:15.139 --> 00:16:20.430
Last time they were here, Jaime was proud
golden lion, and Tyrion a drunken whoremonger.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:25.660
Now Jaime has lost his pride and his hand,
and Tyrion has lost his taste for prostitutes

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:30.730
– this is partly tied to his grief for Shae,
and Tyrion also mentions “self-betterment”

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:34.610
– he’s more focussed now on making a difference
in the world.

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:39.190
Tyrion mentions how mad their father would
be if he knew his sons were fighting for the

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:40.190
Starks.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:45.709
Tywin was brutal in his war to destroy the
Starks and make House Lannister a dynasty

00:16:45.709 --> 00:16:47.560
to last a thousand years.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:53.680
But now, House Lannister’s all but gone,
and it’s the Stark legacy that lives on.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:58.980
Game of Thrones is a dark story where good
guys die, but the message isn’t totally

00:16:58.980 --> 00:16:59.980
bleak.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:06.329
Acts of heroism and love outshine the darkness,
so long as they’re remembered.

00:17:06.329 --> 00:17:09.790
Brienne, Pod, Tormund and Davos join the Lannisters.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.110
Tormund tells a ridiculous story about suckling
on a giant.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:17.640
He’s got heaps of that stuff in the books
– he claims that a bear bit off half his

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:23.150
penis, but that his penis is still twice as
large as anyone else’s . So these unlikely

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:28.290
companions share warmth and wine, in the face
of probable death tomorrow.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:33.950
Meanwhile, the Hound sits alone in the cold
– until Arya comes along.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.180
In Season 4, Arya and the Hound were kindred
spirits.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:41.780
They both use violence and hate to hide their
loneliness and fear.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:46.270
But after they parted ways, the Hound’s
become all heroic, fighting for the good guys,

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:48.180
when he used to only care for himself.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:54.559
Arya asks why he changed, and the Hound replies
that he fought for Arya . It seems that their

00:17:54.559 --> 00:17:58.790
bond taught the Hound that it’s worth fighting
to protect others.

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:03.780
Beric Dondarrion shows up – he used to be
on Arya’s death list for selling Gendry

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:06.570
to Melisandre, but Arya’s let go of that.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:12.610
Beric talks about his god, the Lord of Light,
and says “This is his moment” . The Lord

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:18.520
of Light is all about good versus evil, light
versus dark, all that Zoroastrian stuff.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:23.020
Next episode’s battle for the dawn might
be Beric’s time to fulfil his destiny in

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.590
some fiery sacrifice.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:29.179
In the books, Beric gives up his life force
to resurrect Catelyn.

00:18:29.179 --> 00:18:33.309
So maybe Beric will resurrect someone next
episode.

00:18:33.309 --> 00:18:36.450
Tormund is shocked to learn that Brienne isn’t
a knight.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.210
Because in Westeros, women aren’t allowed
to be knights.

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:44.929
Part of the point of Brienne’s character
is to show how unjust this sexist system is.

00:18:44.929 --> 00:18:50.000
Brienne is more brave and selfless and honourable
than most any actual knight , yet this her

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.600
society denies her knighthood because of her
gender.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:57.630
Tormund calls bullshit on that, and Jaime
makes Brienne a knight.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:02.480
This is the ultimate vindication for Brienne
– the acknowledgement and respect that she’s

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.660
always deserved.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:09.420
It’s also important for Jaime – in many
ways, he was a failed knight, an oathbreaker,

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.230
who hurt innocent people.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:14.220
Now, he raises up a true knight.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:19.640
This is an intimate moment for Brienne and
Jaime – the scene almost feels like a wedding.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:24.299
Jaime declares his faith in Brienne, just
as she did for him before.

00:19:24.299 --> 00:19:30.790
Jaime and Brienne might never kiss or have
sex, but this knighting is a moment of love.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.120
Sam gives Jorah the Valyrian sword Heartsbane.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.610
This was the sword of Sam’s father Randyll.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:41.720
But Randyll was an asshole, and Sam took the
sword to represent his rejection of his father.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:45.950
Instead, Sam says that Jeor Mormont was a
father to him.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:50.320
Jeor was Commander of the Night’s Watch,
and was Jorah’s father.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.830
Jorah failed his father by slaving and leaving
Westeros.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:59.630
But now Sam gives Jorah Heartsbane “to guard
the realms of men” , as Jeor would have

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.630
wanted.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:05.280
So this is another example of a character
whose memory long outlives his death.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:09.890
But it’s also the story of a man who rejects
his biological father and chooses another

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.940
man as his father – which could be relevant
for Jon.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:17.810
Jon is the biological son of Rhaegar, but
Ned Stark is his father.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:21.920
Podrick sings a song about love and loss and
memory.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:26.580
It’s about the ghosts of the friends and
family that these characters have lost, and

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.250
the ghosts of the people they used to be.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:34.700
It’s a moment of bittersweet melancholy,
as they share one last night of love and light

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:41.010
in the face of death and forgetting – a
dream of spring as winter comes . The song

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.790
also ties deeply into the lore.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:48.570
The song is called Jenny’s song, named for
Jenny of Oldstones, a mysterious woman who

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.390
lived fifty years ago.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:55.160
She dwelt among ruins, danced with ghosts,
and wore flowers in her hair.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:59.820
Prince Duncan Targaryen fell in love with
her, and gave up his crown to marry her . Jenny

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:04.320
had a friend who was a witch, and claimed
to be a child of the forest.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:08.610
This witch is still alive in the books, as
the ghost of High Heart, and she makes a bunch

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.850
of accurate prophecies.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:14.831
Back in the day, she prophesied that the prince
that was promised – the hero who’ll save

00:21:14.831 --> 00:21:19.620
the world – will be born of the line of
the Mad King Aerys and his sister.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:23.750
So, they got married, and had Rhaegar Viserys
and Daenerys.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:30.530
Rhaegar was born at the tragic fire of Summerhall,
which killed Prince Duncan, and possibly Jenny.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:35.900
Rhaegar spent his emo teenage years in the
ruins of Summerhall, singing sad songs.

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:39.700
Some fans speculate that Rhaegar may have
written Jenny’s song.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:44.660
This may be the song that Rhaegar played to
woo Lyanna Stark – leading to the birth

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:47.190
of their child Jon.

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:52.570
So Jenny’s song is a thread of prophecy
and melancholy that runs from Jon and Dany

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:55.960
back through Rhaegar and Summerhall to Jenny.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:00.429
And now, Jon reveals to Daenerys that Rhaegar
is his father.

00:22:00.429 --> 00:22:04.590
This means that Daenerys is Jon’s aunt,
and Jon has a better claim to the Throne than

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:05.590
she does.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:10.830
Daenerys has fought for the Throne for seven
seasons, so she’s deeply shaken by Jon’s

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:11.830
claim.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:16.200
Of course, Jon doesn’t want the Throne,
which could tie back to Jenny’s song.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:19.539
Prince Duncan gave up his crown out of love
for Jenny.

00:22:19.539 --> 00:22:22.520
Maybe Jon will give up his crown for Daenerys.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:27.760
Or maybe Daenerys will give up hers – remember
Sam asked last episode if Daenerys would give

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:33.059
up her crown . Alternatively, Jon and Dany
could get married and rule together.

00:22:33.059 --> 00:22:39.620
But such a happy ending seems unlikely – the
white walkers arrive at Winterfell.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:45.931
Jenny’s song, and kind of this whole episode
is about characters haunted by the dead, by

00:22:45.931 --> 00:22:48.930
the metaphorical ghosts of the past.

00:22:48.930 --> 00:22:53.880
But they’re also haunted by a very literal
army of the dead.

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:58.270
The zombies are here, and they’re led by
a lot of white walkers.

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:01.860
Remember, wights are the zombies, and they’re
pretty easy to kill.

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:07.570
But white walkers are the ice people who lead
the dead, and we’ve only seen a few of them.

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:12.600
Now there a dozens or hundreds of walkers
at Winterfell – where did they all come

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:13.600
from?

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:17.870
We know that Craster gave his babies to be
transformed into white walkers, and he was

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:22.820
probably not the only person doing this – there
are wildlings in the far north rumoured to

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:24.950
worship cold gods.

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:29.830
So over thousand of years, the walkers must
have slowly built up these numbers.

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:33.830
The walkers also have zombie giants, and animals
like polar bears.

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.690
There are legends about giant ice spiders.

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:42.090
And the white walkers are led by the Night
King, riding the dragon Viserion – but we

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:43.960
don’t see them here.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:48.500
Some fans speculate that the Night King won’t
join this battle, and instead, he’ll fly

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:53.260
south and attack King’s Landing, turning
its million inhabitants into another army

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:54.550
of the dead.

00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:58.740
This would be similar to the Battle of the
Whispering Wood, when Robb Stark split his

00:23:58.740 --> 00:24:03.340
army, and surprise attacked Jaime – Jaime
mentions the Whispering Wood this episode

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:09.530
. The excellent History of Westeros podcast
points out another possible parallel in Thrones

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:10.530
history.

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:16.370
In the Dance of the Dragons, Aemond Targaryen,
a dragon-rider with a blue sapphire eye , split

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:18.720
from his army and attacked elsewhere.

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:23.990
So Daemon Targaryen and his lover Nettles
chased him down, on their dragons.

00:24:23.990 --> 00:24:28.140
Maybe, similarly, Jon and Daenerys will have
to chase down the Night King.

00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:31.679
But that’s just a guess – we’ll find
out soon.

00:24:31.679 --> 00:24:37.820
This is the second episode of six episode
season, and not very much has happened.

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:40.550
Some fans dismiss this as pointless farnarkling.

00:24:40.550 --> 00:24:45.370
But the point of these episodes is to remind
us why we care about these characters – before

00:24:45.370 --> 00:24:48.290
the next episodes rip them away.

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:53.630
This is Jenny’s song, remembering the ghosts
that give these characters humanity, in the

00:24:53.630 --> 00:24:57.059
face of darkness and death.

00:24:57.059 --> 00:25:01.820
When Brienne is knighted, Tyrion calls her
a “Knight of the Seven Kingdoms”.

00:25:01.820 --> 00:25:06.030
That’s the title of a collection of Game
of Thrones prequel stories about a knight

00:25:06.030 --> 00:25:08.100
called Duncan the Tall.

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:14.380
George Martin has hinted that Dunk is an ancestor
of Brienne – they’re similar characters.

00:25:14.380 --> 00:25:16.320
Like Brienne, Dunk is an underdog.

00:25:16.320 --> 00:25:21.340
He’s not the smartest or the strongest,
and it’s implied he’s not really a knight.

00:25:21.340 --> 00:25:26.950
But he’s brave and honourable, and he upholds
his vows – here’s a quote from the audiobook:

00:25:26.950 --> 00:25:32.090
“He charged me to be a good knight and true,
to obey the seven gods, defend the weak and

00:25:32.090 --> 00:25:38.000
innocent, serve my lord faithfully, and defend
the realm with all my might, and I swore that

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:39.000
I would”.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:43.789
In A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms, Dunk adventures
across Westeros with a Targaryen kid.

00:25:43.789 --> 00:25:49.830
He meets a young three-eyed raven and a young
Walder Frey, and he kisses the woman who becomes

00:25:49.830 --> 00:25:52.549
Jaime Lannister’s great-grandmother.

00:25:52.549 --> 00:25:57.830
You can read all of Dunk’s stories for free
today by signing up for a trial with Audible.

00:25:57.830 --> 00:26:01.780
Members get a book each month, and if you
cancel, you keep the books.

00:26:01.780 --> 00:26:07.070
You can read in the car or the gym or while
drinking and waiting for the apocalypse.

00:26:07.070 --> 00:26:10.740
Sign up at audible.com/asx.

00:26:10.740 --> 00:26:13.900
Thanks for watching, and thanks to the artists
for their work.

00:26:13.900 --> 00:26:19.150
Thanks to the Patrons, including Bloody Tyrant,
Scarlett, Random Vowels, Gina, and Sam Lundin

00:26:19.150 --> 00:26:20.150
of House Vimbly, first of his name, Lord of
Union Square, and Protector of the Realm.

00:26:20.150 --> 00:26:20.151
Cheers.

